# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=cold spec=hunter:marksmanship style=dodge
# size=10 difficulty=normal view=844x390,touch save=fresh. boss=cold is a
# coverage label only -- `evening` steers at no boss (direction.md's own
# repeated note under [[#6]]) -- so this walks in fresh at the door same as
# any other 10-normal evening.
#
# What is actually new here: `dodge` has only ever been run through an
# evening twice before, and both were 25-heroic on a desktop/mouse viewport
# (2026-09-26, paladin:protection; 2026-09-30, paladin:retribution) -- never
# at 10-normal, never on a touch viewport, and never on this spec. That
# matters specifically for THE VIGIL and #271 (the "wipe here and the evening
# never comes back" bug, eleven confirmations across seven specs and four
# other styles at this exact size/difficulty/save cell). Every one of those
# eleven confirmations used a style that actively moves toward or away from
# the boss the whole time (flee runs straight off the boss's own position;
# melee/good/wander/auto all close or wander). Read scripts/playbot.ts before
# writing this: `dodge`'s steering (line ~929) only reacts to what is
# currently underfoot -- `want = away` off the nearest standing hazard, with
# no boss-directed term at all outside `good` -- so in a corridor with no
# ground patches, just chasing watchmen, dodge may not steer *away from the
# watchmen* the way flee does, and could sit still (want=null) until
# something is actually standing on it. That is a genuinely different
# steering shape than every style that has met THE VIGIL's watchmen so far,
# and no session has asked whether #271's wipe shape depends on the style
# actively fleeing the threat versus one that only reacts to hazards already
# under it.
open
targets
shot front

tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:hunter:marksmanship
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
